cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jspassgen-sdk-cpp in research or production write-ups, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "jspassgen-sdk-cpp: the native C++ port of the jspassgen core"
abstract: >-
  The native C++17 port of the jspassgen password and passphrase
  core, drawing every random value from the operating system's CSPRNG.
  It currently provides the random port and its OS backends; the
  generators follow jspassgen's conformance kit.
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
version: "0.0.24"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
# Dual-licensed, at the user's option (LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT).
# CFF 1.2.0 takes SPDX licence identifiers, not an SPDX expression; a
# list of several means the work is available under any of them.
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/jspassgen-sdk-cpp"
url: "https://jspassgen.com"
keywords:
  - password generator
  - CSPRNG
  - C++
  - SDK
